                "entry_id": "542ac43f-154d-39c9-8b39-2c2db295031f",
                "word": "knickerbockers",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "1b5d232f-0614-49b1-9333-c839e6beab83",
                        "entry_id": "542ac43f-154d-39c9-8b39-2c2db295031f",
                        "tags": [
                            "attributive"
                        ],
                        "form": "knickerbocker"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c71448eb-bd9f-33c1-b0b4-a9fc2959d9de",
                        "entry_id": "542ac43f-154d-39c9-8b39-2c2db295031f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Men's or boys' baggy knee breeches, of a type particularly popular in the early 20th century."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "plural-only"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f3c9385a-029b-4f0e-9d85-f72c8074e2bc",
                                "sense_id": "c71448eb-bd9f-33c1-b0b4-a9fc2959d9de",
                                "text": "Five men and a woman, two young girls,[…], and a boy […] are at the machines sewing knickerbockers, “knee-pants” in the Ludlow Street dialect."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3da5dbff-d3d1-43d7-bafe-248652cf81d4",
                                "sense_id": "c71448eb-bd9f-33c1-b0b4-a9fc2959d9de",
                                "text": "[…] and some gems that represent the tasseled garment that the leader wears show it in a distinctly religious connection. On a gem from Zakro it [the sistrum] is being being carried by a man who does not wear the loin-cloth, but a baggy kind of knickerbockers like the Moslem trousers of to-day."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ee841ec7-659b-444a-9496-7356d6e0037e",
                                "sense_id": "c71448eb-bd9f-33c1-b0b4-a9fc2959d9de",
                                "text": "And it was early morning, and the world was moist, when the crystal-gazer's husband, a freak in knickerbockers with an open coppish and a sabbath gamp, came over the stones outside his house to meet the holy travellers."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2ab04b3a-d00b-499e-8168-fcfb96d397d4",
                        "source_entry_id": "542ac43f-154d-39c9-8b39-2c2db295031f",
                        "source_sense_id": "c71448eb-bd9f-33c1-b0b4-a9fc2959d9de",
                        "source_sense_description": "knickerbockers",
                        "target_lang_word": "knickerbocker",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "knickerbocker",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7a1c674e-54eb-398e-93f2-830ab868dd64",
                                        "entry_id": "a7317ff8-7f2f-3992-8783-ebef79b56581",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "wijde korte broek wa"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "decd53b0-8f0c-40e6-9f8c-6c8ee2d12579",
                                                "sense_id": "7a1c674e-54eb-398e-93f2-830ab868dd64",
                                                "text": "Op de Hazeltine National Golf Club in Chaska Minnesota, waar gisteren het PGA Championship is begonnen, ligt een plaquette die herinnert aan de meest markante golfer die de Verenigde Staten heeft gekend. Payne Stewart speelde altijd in een knickerbocker en een trui in afwisselende kleurstellingen. En hij droeg ook een ouderwetse pet. Andere golfers kleedden zich volgens de regels. Stewart wilde anders zijn. Hij was anders."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8abc0f5-c4de-4a2a-86c6-f57997f05b2d",
                                                "sense_id": "7a1c674e-54eb-398e-93f2-830ab868dd64",
                                                "text": "Alleen Nancy Reagan wist er binnen het protocol nog een feest van te maken qua geldsmijterij en het inhuren van een glamoureuze modeontwerper om haar magere poppenlijfje tiptop in te pakken. In Reagans geval was dat James Galanos, hofleverancier van Diana Ross, die Nancy consequent Dynasty-waardig kleedde en slechts één keer uit de bocht vloog: toen hij Mrs. President in een met kralen opgesierde knickerbocker naar de Amerikaanse ambassade in Parijs liet gaan."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4adf4a97-fe7d-40b4-a30d-0cfd21e6311f",
                        "source_entry_id": "542ac43f-154d-39c9-8b39-2c2db295031f",
                        "source_sense_id": "c71448eb-bd9f-33c1-b0b4-a9fc2959d9de",
